 {
  "uri": "http://kulturarvsdata.se/SMVK-MM/arkiv/5367900",
  "url": "https://collections.smvk.se/carlotta-mhm/web/object/5367900",
  "label": "email, e-post",
  "org": "SMVK-MM",
  "desc": [
   [
    "Text in document",
    "Good afternoon,\n\nI am a postgraduate student and researcher with the University of Manchester, England. My current research is on Predynastic and Early Dynastic Egyptian flint figures, specifically animal representations. I am intending to publish a catalogued corpus of these objects as to make them accessible for further research and study. \n\nWhile looking through your collection I identified four fantastic examples of bird flints (MM10477; MM10471; MM10476; MME1969:718)\n\nI have also been able to identify five further objects which are of great interest to my research:\nhttps://collections.smvk.se/carlotta-mhm/web/object/3015309\nhttps://collections.smvk.se/carlotta-mhm/web/object/3015283\nhttps://collections.smvk.se/carlotta-mhm/web/object/3015332\nhttps://collections.smvk.se/carlotta-mhm/web/object/3015344\nhttps://collections.smvk.se/carlotta-mhm/web/object/3015308\nThese were all donated by Major R.G.Gayer-Anderson along with two of the avian form flints. \n\nI believe that these first three objects represent crocodiles or reptiles, and I have so far been able to collect 13 other examples of this. The latter two, especially the last, may be abstract representations of this also. \n\nUnfortunately, I have not been able to search your collection to the extent which I wish to, so I would like to kindly request your help. Would you be able to assist me in checking your collection for further objects which are in these forms? A focus on the donations of Gayer-Anderson may be needed, as it seems he definitely had an preference for this type of object! I am more than happy to send you some examples of differing animal forms if this would be of assistance to you.\n\nWith many kind regards,\n\nJenna Hiscock\nimage.png\nGraduate Alumna - Swansea University, Wales\nPostgraduate Student - University of Manchester, England"
   ]
  ],
